       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. Amlodipine 50 mg is also well above the 10 mg labeled maximum daily dose, so a confirmation I can't check doesn't change my answer.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range now.** For example, amlodipine 10 mg by mouth once daily, which is the maximum. I can add a note on the order that the specialist recommended escalation.\n- **Add a second agent.** If standard dosing failed, the usual next step is a different class, such as an ACE inhibitor or ARB, or a thiazide-like diuretic, rather than a much higher amlodipine dose. The specialist may have a plan for this.\n- **Route the high dose through pharmacy.** If the specialist really wants 50 mg, pharmacy and the prescriber can review and enter it through the hospital's process for exceeding maximum doses. That process would include a documented override and monitoring.\n\nDo you want me to enter the 10 mg order?"
